From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 15:53:50 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: imx8mq: Restore the syscon compatible on anatop

Commit f98c2dfedb73 ("arm64: dts: imx8m: align anatop with bindings")
dropped "syscon" from the anatop node. Consumers reaching the block with
syscon_regmap_lookup_by_compatible() have failed ever since, including
the PCIe driver configuring the internal PLL as REF_CLK, which leaves
the port without a reference clock.

Restore the compatible; the node keeps its clock-controller role.

Fixes: f98c2dfedb73 ("arm64: dts: imx8m: align anatop with bindings")
Signed-off-by: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq.dtsi
index b28840d..5aade41 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq.dtsi
@@ -809,7 +809,7 @@
 			};
 
 			anatop: clock-controller@30360000 {
-				compatible = "fsl,imx8mq-anatop";
+				compatible = "fsl,imx8mq-anatop", "syscon";
 				reg = <0x30360000 0x10000>;
 				interrupts = <GIC_SPI 49 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 				#clock-cells = <1>;
